  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.0.38\"\n\npackage:\n  name: mecatl\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/stacklok/mecatl/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 2630df20bae98f512fcccdf82f9e25f066c1a5b04716c3605039a263035c66e1\n  target_directory: src\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip:\n    - win\n  script:\n    - cd src\n    - go-licenses save ./cmd/mecated ./cmd/mecatui --save_path ../library_licenses --ignore github.com/stacklok/mecatl --ignore github.com/segmentio/asm --ignore go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/jaeger\n    - go build -v -o $PREFIX/bin/mecated -ldflags=\"-s -w\" ./cmd/mecated\n    - go build -v -o $PREFIX/bin/mecatui -ldflags=\"-s -w\" ./cmd/mecatui\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler(\"go-nocgo\") }}\n    - go-licenses\n\ntests:\n  - script: mecated --help\n  - script: mecatui --help\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - mecated\n        - mecatui\n      strict: true\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/stacklok/mecatl\n  summary: Open source, cloud-native agent harness (server + terminal client)\n  description: |\n    Mecatl is an open source, cloud-native agent harness. It provides the\n    loop, tools, permissions, hooks, delegation, and service boundaries for\n    running AI agents as production workloads on infrastructure you operate.\n\n    This package installs mecated (the server) and mecatui (the terminal\n    client), matching the project's official Homebrew formula. Other\n    binaries in the repository (mecak8s, mecatequi, mecademo) are not\n    included; see the upstream README for building those from source.\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - src/LICENSE\n    - library_licenses/\n  documentation: https://mecatl.dev/docs\n  repository: https://github.com/stacklok/mecatl\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - keponk\n",
